  "details": "The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Corinthia-Epidauros border",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The peak of Halieion was located in the Corinthia near the border of Epidauros. Its name figures in a Hellenistic-period inscription (IG IV\u00b2,1 71) now located in Epidauros that outlines boundaries when one Aigialeos was the strat\u00e8gos of the Achaians.",
